---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **BTS 일곱 명의 별자리, 그리고 그것이 우연인지.** (`/bts-star-signs`)
 *
 * ⭐ 사장님 표준 작업틀의 첫 지면이다 — 「남의 이슈 + 우리만의 축」.
 *   전문: docs/작업틀-이슈더하기우리축.md
 *   이슈  BTS 아리랑 영국 오피셜 앨범 차트 24주째 (스포츠월드 제목)
 *   축    우리가 가진 한국 연예인 9,249명의 생일 → 별자리 분포
 *
 * ── 🔴 이 지면이 절대 안 하는 것 ─────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ **풀이를 하지 않는다.** 「염소자리라서 …」는 강령에 정면으로 걸린다.
 * ⛔ **「특별한 배치」라고 쓰지 않는다.** 재 보면 여섯 가지가 가장 흔한 결과(38.7%)다.
 * ⛔ **영국 차트를 우리가 잰 것처럼 쓰지 않는다.** 그것은 온 «까닭»이지 우리 수가 아니다.
 * ⭐ 우리가 내는 것은 둘 — 일곱 명의 자리(사실)와, 그것이 우연 안인지(위험).
 *
 * 🔴 Astro 앞말은 TypeScript 다. 🔴 JSX 는 끝 공백을 버린다 — {' '} 를 쓴다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import KcwMethodLimits from '../../components/KcwMethodLimits.astro';
import d from '../../data/kcw-bts-signs.json';

/* 🔴 제목에 박은 수가 자료와 어긋나면 «빌드를 세운다» — 자료가 바뀌면 제목이
   조용히 거짓이 된다. cap-per-artist·staying-power 에서 쓴 것과 같은 장치다. */
if (d.서로다른자리 !== 6) {
  throw new Error(`제목이 「여섯 자리」라고 말하는데 자료는 ${d.서로다른자리} 다.`);
}
const 처녀자리 = d.멤버.filter((m: any) => m.자리 === 'Virgo').map((m: any) => m.이름);
if (처녀자리.length !== 2 || !처녀자리.includes('RM') || !처녀자리.includes('Jung Kook')) {
  throw new Error(`겹치는 자리가 RM·Jung Kook 의 처녀자리가 아니다 — ${JSON.stringify(처녀자리)}`);
}

const 큰자리 = [...d.자리별].sort((a: any, b: any) => b.사람 - a.사람);
const 가장많은 = 큰자리[0];
const 가장적은 = 큰자리[큰자리.length - 1];
const 잡음밖 = d.자리별.filter((x: any) => x.잡음밖인가);
const 빽빽한달 = [...d.달별].sort((a: any, b: any) => b.하루당 - a.하루당)[0];
const 성긴달 = [...d.달별].sort((a: any, b: any) => a.하루당 - b.하루당)[0];
const 달이름 = ['January', 'February', 'March', 'April', 'May', 'June',
  'July', 'August', 'September', 'October', 'November', 'December'];

const TITLE = 'BTS star signs: six signs for seven members, and that is the ordinary result';
const DESC =
  `Jin is a Sagittarius, Suga a Pisces, J-Hope an Aquarius, RM and Jung Kook both Virgos, `
  + `Jimin a Libra, V a Capricorn. Six distinct signs among seven members — which is the single `
  + `most likely outcome (${d.이배치가나올확률}%) when you draw seven people from the `
  + `${d.사람총수.toLocaleString('en-US')} Korean entertainers whose birth dates we hold.`;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://www.wikidata.org/'],
  variableMeasured: ['star sign', 'date of birth', 'distance from chance in standard deviations'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/bts-star-signs">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    Seven members. Six signs. RM and Jung Kook are both Virgos and nobody else overlaps.
  </p>

  <p class="walk">
    <b>Next:</b>{' '}
    <a href="/star-signs">Which Korean stars share your Chinese zodiac sign</a> &middot;{' '}
    <a href="/member-vs-group">Members and their groups</a> &middot;{' '}
    <a href="/kpop-birthdays">K-pop birthdays by month</a>
  </p>

  <table>
    <caption>The seven members, by date of birth</caption>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Member</th><th>Name</th><th>Born</th><th>Sign</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {d.멤버.map((m: any) => (
        <tr>
          <td><b>{m.이름}</b></td>
          <td>{m.본명}</td>
          <td>{m.태어난날}</td>
          <td>{m.자리}</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Six of seven is not unusual. It is the most likely answer</h2>

  <p>
    We drew seven people at random from the {d.사람총수.toLocaleString('en-US')} Korean
    entertainers whose birth dates we hold, 200,000 times, using the real distribution rather
    than a flat one. Here is how many distinct signs came out.
  </p>

  <table>
    <caption>Distinct signs among seven people drawn at random (200,000 draws, seed 20260905)</caption>
    <thead><tr><th>Distinct signs</th><th>Share of draws</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {d.뽑기분포.map((x: any) => (
        <tr class={x.가지 === d.서로다른자리 ? 'hit' : undefined}>
          <td>{x.가지}</td>
          <td>{x.몫}%</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p class="q">
    <b>{d.이배치가나올확률}% of random groups of seven land on six distinct signs.</b>{' '}
    It is the most common outcome — though only just: five distinct signs comes up in
    {' '}{d.뽑기분포.find((x: any) => x.가지 === 5).몫}% of draws, and the two are close enough
    that a different seven people could easily have landed there instead.
    Whatever is interesting about these seven people,
    their spread across the zodiac is not it.
  </p>

  <h2>The unusual thing is not BTS. It is the whole population</h2>

  <p>
    While checking that, a real gap turned up — not in the band, but in the
    {' '}{d.사람총수.toLocaleString('en-US')} people behind it. If birthdays fell evenly across the
    twelve signs, each would hold about {가장많은.기대.toLocaleString('en-US')} people, and chance
    alone would move that by roughly 27 either way. It moves a great deal more.
  </p>

  <table>
    <caption>
      Korean entertainers by star sign, and how far each sits from an even spread
    </caption>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Sign</th><th>People</th><th>Expected</th><th>Distance from chance</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {큰자리.map((x: any) => (
        <tr class={x.잡음밖인가 ? 'hit' : undefined}>
          <td>{x.자리}</td>
          <td>{x.사람.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
          <td>{x.기대.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
          <td>{x.표준편차 > 0 ? `+${x.표준편차}` : x.표준편차} sd</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    <b>{가장많은.자리} holds {가장많은.사람.toLocaleString('en-US')} and
    {' '}{가장적은.자리} holds {가장적은.사람.toLocaleString('en-US')}</b> — a gap of
    {' '}{(가장많은.사람 / 가장적은.사람).toFixed(2)} to one, far outside what chance produces.
    {' '}{잡음밖.length} of the twelve signs sit more than two standard deviations from an even
    spread.
  </p>

  <p class="q">
    This is a fact about Korean birth records, not about star signs.
    {' '}<b>{달이름[빽빽한달.달 - 1]} is the densest month at {빽빽한달.하루당} people per day;
    {' '}{달이름[성긴달.달 - 1]} is the thinnest at {성긴달.하루당}.</b>{' '}
    Winter and early spring carry more births than summer does, and the signs simply inherit that.
  </p>

  <h2>One number in this table is partly an artefact</h2>

  <p>
    {d.새해첫날인사람} people in our source are recorded as born on <b>1 January</b>. That is the
    date used when only a year of birth is known, so it is not {d.새해첫날인사람} real
    New Year's Day births. Capricorn is shown twice below for that reason.
  </p>

  <table>
    <caption>Capricorn, as counted and with 1 January removed</caption>
    <thead><tr><th>Counted</th><th>Without 1 January</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>{d.자리별.find((x: any) => x.자리 === 'Capricorn').사람.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
        <td>{d.자리별.find((x: any) => x.자리 === 'Capricorn').새해첫날뺀것.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    Pisces is not affected by that date and still sits furthest from chance. So the pattern
    survives the artefact, which is the only reason we are willing to describe it at all.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we looked at this today</h2>

  <p>
    A Korean sports daily reported this week that BTS's <i>Arirang</i> was in its 24th week on the
    UK Official Albums Chart. <b>We did not measure that chart and we make no claim about it.</b>{' '}
    It is the reason we opened the file, not a number of ours. What we can measure is who these
    seven people are in the data we hold, and whether anything about that is out of the ordinary.
  </p>

  <p class="q">
    The answer is no — and saying so is the point.
    {' '}<b>This is a statistic, not a person.</b> We do not tell you what a sign means, because a
    date of birth does not carry that information and pretending otherwise would make us a
    fortune teller rather than a map.
  </p>

  {/* ⚠ 이 조각은 method·limitation·note 만 받는다. 자료의 «못잰것»은 배열이라
      그대로 넘기면 안 나온다 — 아래 목록으로 직접 낸다. */}
  <KcwMethodLimits
    method={{
      'What this is': d.whatThisIs,
      'Source': d.출처.join(' · '),
      'Chance test': '200,000 draws of seven people from the real distribution, seed 20260905',
    }}
    limitation={{
      'What this is not': d.whatThisIsNot.join(' '),
    }} />

  <h2>What we could not measure</h2>
  <ul>
    {d.못잰것.map((x: any) => (<li>{x}</li>))}
  </ul>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/bts-star-signs" />
</WikiTip>

<style>
  .lead { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .q { background: #f6f7f9; border-left: 3px solid #999; padding: .7rem .9rem; margin: 1rem 0; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 1rem 0; font-size: .95rem; }
  caption { text-align: left; font-weight: 600; padding-bottom: .4rem; }
  th, td { border-bottom: 1px solid #e3e5e8; padding: .4rem .6rem; text-align: left; }
  th { background: #fafbfc; }
  tr.hit td { background: #fff8e6; font-weight: 600; }
  .walk { font-size: .95rem; margin: .6rem 0 1.2rem; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    .q { background: #1c1f24; border-left-color: #666; }
    th { background: #1a1d21; }
    th, td { border-bottom-color: #2a2e34; }
    tr.hit td { background: #2b2617; }
  }
</style>
